# A clone of the prototype's public repository, which the evidence ledger reads
# its proofs from; it is recreated whenever it is missing.
/.cache/

# The paper's build output, made anew by `just research paper-a`.
/paper-a/build/

# The binaries `go build` leaves where it is run: the research's tools are run
# with `go run`, and a built one is never kept.
/citecheck
/ledger
/macros
/isolation
/tools/*/citecheck
/tools/*/ledger
/tools/*/macros
/tools/*/isolation
/faultinject
/learnersim

# Copies of local files the repository keeps out — the product's planning
# documents and the prototype's — kept as this machine's memory of what they
# said, never as evidence.
/archive/

# The numbers the paper prints, written anew from the results by every build of
# the paper and of the artifact, and the version the named build prints.
/paper-a/generated/

# The artifact as it is assembled and unpacked, made anew by
# `just research release`.
/release/build/
